    bio: "Masayoshi Son was born in Tosu, Saga Prefecture, Japan, to a poor Korean family. His grandfather was a Korean immigrant who came to Japan illegally by boat. Son grew up in poverty.\n\nAt 16, he moved to California alone to study English. He attended UC Berkeley, where he earned a degree in economics in three years by taking extra courses. He returned to Japan and founded SoftBank in 1981.\n\nHis $100 billion Vision Fund reshaped venture capital. He lost $70 billion in the dot-com crash but rebuilt. His audacious bets have made him a legendary figure in global tech investing.",
